# Cloud Storage Non-Hydration Invariant

You are operating within the `{{project_name}}` workspace. When evaluating cloud-synced storage (Dropbox, Google Drive, Box via macOS FileProvider):

## 1. Non-Hydration Enforcement
- Never execute commands (`file`, `du -sh`, `xxh64sum`, `md5`, `ffprobe`) that trigger on-demand hydration of dataless stubs to the local boot drive.
- Use non-hydrating metadata discovery (`ls -leO`, `stat`, or non-reading file queries).
- Do not write temporary files or audit scratch logs to target volumes.
